Section: {{ section_id }}

Verify every claim unit below against the evidence excerpts attached to its citations. For each
unit decide whether the cited evidence actually entails the sentence, whether the citation scope
matches the claim, and whether the sentence overclaims beyond the excerpt.

Judgments: `supported` (fully entailed), `partial` (excerpt supports only part of the sentence),
`unsupported` (excerpt does not entail it), `unverifiable` (no usable excerpt / cannot tell).
Assign severity `info|minor|major|blocking` (unsupported factual overclaims are blocking).

{% if sources %}
Source provenance:
{% for sid, source in sources.items() %}- {{ sid }}: tier={{ source.tier }} role={{ source.role }} access={{ source.access_mode }} peer_reviewed={{ source.peer_reviewed }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Cited claim units:
{% for sentence in sentences %}
- id={{ sentence.id }}
  text: {{ sentence.text }}
  cited: {{ sentence.cited_keys | join(', ') }}
  evidence:
{% for ev in sentence.evidence %}
    * [{{ ev.claim_id }}] source={{ ev.source_ids | join(', ') }} origin={{ ev.origin }} tier={{ ev.tier }} locator={{ ev.locator }}
      excerpt: {{ ev.excerpt }}
{% endfor %}
{% if not sentence.evidence %}
    * (no retrieved excerpt for these citations)
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if uncited %}
Uncited factual sentences (decide whether each needs a citation; list the ids that do):
{% for unit in uncited %}
- id={{ unit.id }}: {{ unit.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Return one result per sentence id above, with the judgment, a short rationale and a severity.
List the ids of unsupported sentences in `unsupported_claims`, partial ones in `partial_claims`,
and uncited sentences that need a source in `uncited_factual`. Quote nothing else.
